SUMMARY:Chiques Creek Watershed Alliance - Clean Water Day at Governor Dick Park
DESCRIPTION:On Sep 19\, CCWA is collaborating with the Clarence Schock Memorial Park at Governor Dick\, and with The Lebanon Valley Conservancy\, in a ‘Clean Water Day at Governor Dick Park.’ (https://www.chiquescreekwatershedalliance.org/upcoming/clean-water-day-at-governor-dick-park).  This is part of TLVC Clean Water Week.\n\nWe are thrilled to have 3 highly regarded speakers address how agricultural best practices help conserve soil and improve water quality.  Are you curious how ag and other development impact our water\, or what can be done to build resilience? \n\n\nJim Hershey\, a conservation-minded farmer and and award-winning pioneer in agricultural best practices in the Chiques Creek Watershed \n\n\nReid Garner\, environmental engineer / entrepreneur experienced in designing ag and municipal BMP’s \n\n\nMatt Kofroth\, Assistant District Manager at the Lancaster County Conservation District. Helps align potential conservation-oriented ag projects with funding and assesses their impact. \n\n\nFor younger kiddos\, we’ll have a conservation story hour plus some watercolor painting\, and a raffle for a few bluebird houses!  And then for those interested\, a Paw Paw Walk – guided hike to hunt for some of this native fruit! \n\nRegister here for this informative and fun event:  https://www.parkatgovernordick.org/#special-events/clean-water-week.  And please share this event info with others that might be interested.
URL:https://lancasterwatersheds.org/event/chiques-creek-watershed-alliance-clean-water-day-at-governor-dick-park/
LOCATION:Clarence Schock Memorial Park at Governor Dick\, 3283 Pinch Road\, Mt. Gretna\, PA\, 17064\, United States
END:VEVENT
